# Comments for implicit reasons

**Exported hooks, components, and functions:** add a one- or two-sentence JSDoc when the job or a constraint is not obvious from the name. Model: `usePdfPages.ts`, `PageCanvas.tsx`. Skip JSDoc that only repeats the identifier.

**Inline comments:** add a short note when the code is correct for a reason the next reader would not see:

- Pointer capture so drag continues when the pointer leaves the element
- Resetting a zoom anchor so the next zoom must set it again
- Ctrl/Cmd wheel vs plain scroll (trackpad pinch sets `ctrlKey`)
- Generation counters so stale async results cannot overwrite newer state

Comment the **constraint**, not the statement. Do not comment straightforward assignments, early returns, or JSX.

Keep comments next to the line they explain. A few lines is enough; the `PageCanvas` render-cancellation JSDoc is the upper bound for length.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — restates the code
el.scrollLeft = next.scrollLeft;

// ✅ GOOD — explains why
/* capture the pointer so we can move the page without losing it
 * when the pointer leaves the element */
el.setPointerCapture(event.pointerId);
```
